 "section_summary": "This section comprises diplomatic reports, despatches, and Department of State memoranda concerning Japanese internal developments, military operations, and foreign relations from June through August 1938. The principal documents are the Tokyo Embassy's comprehensive monthly political reports for June 1938 (Report No. 141) and July 1938 (Report No. 142), highlighting intensive American diplomatic protests regarding Japanese violations of treaty rights, assaults on U.S. citizens, bombings of mission properties, extraterritorial status, and commercial restrictions in China. The section also includes schedules of despatches and telegrams sent to Washington during June 1938, Despatch No. 3177 transmitting the July report, and Division of Far Eastern Affairs memoranda reviewing the July and August political reports.",
