   "start_page": 185,
   "summary": "This document contains the concluding portion of the Tokyo Embassy's monthly political report for June 1938 (Report No. 141), together with annexed schedules of despatches and telegrams sent during the month. It documents extensive American and British representations concerning Japanese military assaults on nationals (Dr. Thomson, Mrs. Massie), bombings of foreign missions, restrictions on Yangtze navigation, and Japanese challenges to extraterritoriality. The report also details Japanese military progress and air raids in China, international relations with Britain, France, Soviet Russia, Germany, Italy, Australia, and Siam, domestic political changes including the appointment of War Minister Itagaki, and stringent state controls over finance, trade, and 32 key raw materials.",
