   "start_page": 227,
   "summary": "This internal memorandum prepared by Frank A. Schuler, Jr. in the Division of Far Eastern Affairs highlights noteworthy items from the Tokyo Embassy's political report for August 1938. It notes South Manchurian Railway control over coal mining in Shantung, the East Asia Agricultural and Forestry Council's comprehensive agrarian policy, rumors of a Japanese single-party movement, and bureaucratic divergences between the military, Foreign Office, and Finance Ministry regarding the projected 'China Organ'.",
   "title": "Tokyo's political report for August",
