   "summary": "This memorandum prepared by Frank A. Schuler, Jr. in the Division of Far Eastern Affairs summarizes important developments reported in Tokyo's political report for July 1938. It highlights Japanese press assertions regarding British aid to Chiang Kai-shek, tripartite trade negotiations between Japan, Germany, and Manchukuo, impending Polish recognition of Manchukuo, the establishment of the Latin American Cultural Association in Tokyo, and Premier Konoe's proposal for an 'inner cabinet' of ministers without portfolio.",
