   "summary": "This subfile contains the index and opening sections of the Tokyo Embassy's Report No. 142 on conditions in Japan during July 1938. It centers on an extensive two-hour conference on July 4 between Ambassador Joseph C. Grew and Foreign Minister Ugaki Kazushige, along with subsequent representations regarding the Open Door, civilian bombings, and specific grievances. Key issues covered include the local settlement of the Massie slapping incident in Tsingtao, the Peiping embargo on hides and skins, the evacuation and delayed reopening of the University of Shanghai, detention of wood oil owned by the Werner G. Smith Company, an oil monopoly in Kalgan, and U.S. objections to Japanese special military taxation.",
